# Golden files are compared byte-for-byte against LF-joined strings built
# in-process, so they must check out with LF on every platform. Without
# this, a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF and the comparison fails
# over line endings alone (see crates/axilog-schema/tests/v1_shape.rs).
*.golden.txt text eol=lf

# The HTML report embeds these assets verbatim via include_str!, and
# golden_html.rs gates the rendered report against a 600KB budget with only
# ~400 bytes of headroom. A CRLF checkout adds one byte per line (2,009 lines
# across report.css/report.js/skeleton.html), pushing the render to 601,617
# bytes and failing the budget on Windows only -- and making the shipped
# report differ byte-for-byte by build platform, which the crate's own
# determinism tests otherwise promise it does not.
crates/axilog-html/assets/** text eol=lf
